WEBVTT

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:18.635
<v Host>Welcome to Japanese Daily News. I'm Maya. Today is May twenty-sixth. Today's story is big: the Japanese government wants to cut the sales tax on food all the way down to zero. This affects everyone who eats in Japan. Let's listen.

00:00:19.236 --> 00:00:27.899
<v News>日本政府は、食料品の消費税をゼロパーセントにする方針を発表しました。

00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:44.368
<v News>今、日本の消費税は10パーセントです。食料品は8パーセントの軽減税率が適用されています。これをゼロにする計画です。

00:00:45.067 --> 00:01:00.692
<v News>高市早苗首相は、「物価が高くなって、国民の生活が苦しくなっている。食べ物の税金をなくすことで、家計を助けたい」と話しました。

00:01:01.392 --> 00:01:15.959
<v News>この減税は二年間の期間限定です。まず、国会で法案を提出して、早ければ二千二十六年度中に始まる予定です。

00:01:16.659 --> 00:01:30.340
<v News>例えば、今まで百八円だったおにぎりが、百円になります。千八十円だった食料品の買い物が、千円になります。

00:01:31.040 --> 00:01:42.799
<v News>ただし、お酒と外食は対象外です。スーパーやコンビニで買う食べ物と飲み物だけが対象になります。

00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:52.835
<v News>野党からは、「ゼロではなく、すべての消費税を下げるべきだ」という意見も出ています。

00:01:53.536 --> 00:01:55.168
<v Host>Let's break it down.

00:01:55.768 --> 00:01:57.328
<v Host>The opening line.

00:01:57.927 --> 00:02:07.816
<v Slow>日本政府は、食料品の消費税をゼロパーセントにする方針を発表しました。

00:02:08.616 --> 00:02:15.864
<v Host>The Japanese government announced a plan to make the sales tax on food zero percent. Let's look at the key words.

00:02:16.463 --> 00:02:19.199
<v Vocab>食料品

00:02:19.599 --> 00:02:26.319
<v Host>Food products, groceries. This covers rice, vegetables, snacks. Anything you eat.

00:02:26.919 --> 00:02:29.463
<v Vocab>消費税

00:02:29.864 --> 00:02:37.111
<v Host>Consumption tax. Japan calls its sales tax this way. Right now it's ten percent on most things.

00:02:37.711 --> 00:02:40.039
<v Vocab>方針

00:02:40.439 --> 00:02:48.431
<v Host>Policy or plan. When the government uses this word, it means they've decided on a direction but haven't passed a law yet.

00:02:49.032 --> 00:02:50.903
<v Host>The current situation.

00:02:51.503 --> 00:02:59.639
<v Slow>食料品は8パーセントの軽減税率が適用されています。

00:03:00.439 --> 00:03:04.951
<v Host>A reduced tax rate of eight percent is being applied to food products.

00:03:05.551 --> 00:03:08.623
<v Vocab>軽減税率

00:03:09.024 --> 00:03:17.759
<v Host>Reduced tax rate. The first part means reduction. The second part means tax rate. Together: a lightened tax rate.

00:03:18.360 --> 00:03:19.919
<v Host>Why does this matter?

00:03:20.520 --> 00:03:27.864
<v Slow>物価が高くなって、国民の生活が苦しくなっている。

00:03:28.663 --> 00:03:33.271
<v Host>Prices have gone up, and people's daily lives have become difficult.

00:03:33.872 --> 00:03:36.032
<v Vocab>物価

00:03:36.431 --> 00:03:43.919
<v Host>Price level. Not the price of one item, but prices in general. Very common in news about economics.

00:03:44.520 --> 00:03:46.919
<v Vocab>苦しい

00:03:47.319 --> 00:03:53.872
<v Host>Tough, painful, difficult. Used for physical pain, but also financial hardship.

00:03:54.472 --> 00:03:56.415
<v Host>A concrete example.

00:03:57.015 --> 00:04:03.807
<v Slow>今まで百八円だったおにぎりが、百円になります。

00:04:04.608 --> 00:04:14.903
<v Host>An onigiri that cost one hundred and eight yen will become one hundred yen. Eight yen doesn't sound like much, but it adds up across every grocery trip.

00:04:15.503 --> 00:04:17.807
<v Vocab>今まで

00:04:18.208 --> 00:04:25.552
<v Host>Until now. A time expression you'll use constantly. It marks the before in a before-and-after comparison.

00:04:26.151 --> 00:04:27.687
<v Host>But there's a catch.

00:04:28.288 --> 00:04:34.024
<v Slow>ただし、お酒と外食は対象外です。

00:04:34.824 --> 00:04:38.351
<v Host>However, alcohol and eating out are excluded.

00:04:38.951 --> 00:04:41.255
<v Vocab>ただし

00:04:41.656 --> 00:04:49.408
<v Host>However. This is the formal version. In news and official documents, you'll always hear this word.

00:04:50.007 --> 00:04:52.600
<v Vocab>対象外

00:04:53.000 --> 00:05:02.384
<v Host>Outside the scope, excluded. Remove the last character and it means target or covered. So only groceries you take home are included.

00:05:02.983 --> 00:05:05.576
<v Host>And the opposition had something to say.

00:05:06.175 --> 00:05:14.576
<v Slow>野党からは、すべての消費税を下げるべきだという意見も出ています。

00:05:15.375 --> 00:05:20.896
<v Host>The opposition parties say they should lower all consumption tax, not just on food.

00:05:21.495 --> 00:05:23.656
<v Vocab>べきだ

00:05:24.055 --> 00:05:30.680
<v Host>Should do. It expresses a strong opinion. Very common in news and editorials.

00:05:31.279 --> 00:05:34.279
<v Host>Let's listen to the full story one more time.

00:05:34.879 --> 00:05:43.543
<v News>日本政府は、食料品の消費税をゼロパーセントにする方針を発表しました。

00:05:44.244 --> 00:06:00.012
<v News>今、日本の消費税は10パーセントです。食料品は8パーセントの軽減税率が適用されています。これをゼロにする計画です。

00:06:00.711 --> 00:06:16.336
<v News>高市早苗首相は、「物価が高くなって、国民の生活が苦しくなっている。食べ物の税金をなくすことで、家計を助けたい」と話しました。

00:06:17.036 --> 00:06:31.603
<v News>この減税は二年間の期間限定です。まず、国会で法案を提出して、早ければ二千二十六年度中に始まる予定です。

00:06:32.303 --> 00:06:45.983
<v News>例えば、今まで百八円だったおにぎりが、百円になります。千八十円だった食料品の買い物が、千円になります。

00:06:46.684 --> 00:06:58.444
<v News>ただし、お酒と外食は対象外です。スーパーやコンビニで買う食べ物と飲み物だけが対象になります。

00:06:59.144 --> 00:07:08.480
<v News>野党からは、「ゼロではなく、すべての消費税を下げるべきだ」という意見も出ています。

00:07:09.180 --> 00:07:11.915
<v Host>Quiz time. Three questions.

00:07:12.516 --> 00:07:19.235
<v Slow>今、食料品の消費税は何パーセントですか？

00:07:20.036 --> 00:07:26.108
<v Host>What is the current sales tax on food? Eight percent. The plan is to take it to zero.

00:07:26.708 --> 00:07:30.283
<v Slow>お酒は対象ですか？

00:07:31.084 --> 00:07:35.115
<v Host>Is alcohol included? No. It's excluded.

00:07:35.716 --> 00:07:40.108
<v Slow>この減税は何年間ですか？

00:07:40.908 --> 00:07:44.939
<v Host>How many years will this tax cut last? Two years.

00:07:45.540 --> 00:07:57.923
<v Host>That's today's Japanese Daily News. Full transcript with furigana at podcast.jpnotes.dev. Subscribe on Apple Podcasts or Spotify. See you tomorrow.

00:07:58.524 --> 00:08:00.779
<v News>また明日。
